window.docContents[64].resolve({"/rules/RG1006/#RG1006-configuration":{"contents":"No source option, attribute or command-line flag makes this rule pass on a claimed surface. set_option linter.regula false and regula.localFoundation never waive it: lake lint, the build-lint policy target and axiomGate still apply the rule. Where Regula's local linter reports a finding during a project build (axiomGate and the policy target keep it on by default; lake lint builds with it off, whatever the source sets linter.regula to), that finding is a build warning, so the result is INCOMPLETE under RG2003 instead of carrying this rule's finding. Switching the local linter off changes which finding is reported, never whether the result is accepted. Hiding the diagnostic does not establish the property it checks.\n\npartial_fixpoint helpers are not covered by the recursive-helper exception.\n\nProject enforcement runs through lake lint (incremental), lake lint -- --fresh and lake exe axiomGate (fresh whole-project audits from empty build output), and the build-lint policy target. See the adoption guide.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG1006: Unsafe and partial declarations require exact helper authentication","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/RG1006/#RG1006-configuration"},"/rules/RG2005/#RG2005-configuration":{"contents":"No option waives admission. A failed generated-role authentication cannot waive RG1001 or RG1006.\n\nProject enforcement runs through lake lint (incremental), lake lint -- --fresh and lake exe axiomGate (fresh whole-project audits from empty build output), and the build-lint policy target. See the adoption guide.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG2005: Required admission and source evidence must be complete","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/RG2005/#RG2005-configuration"},"/rules/RG4003/#RG4003-configuration":{"contents":"The marker and its pattern are the configuration; there is no option that accepts a non-failing negative example.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG4003: Negative examples require completed intended rejection","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/RG4003/#RG4003-configuration"},"/rules/RG5002/#RG5002-configuration":{"contents":"No source option or command-line flag makes this rule pass on a claimed surface. set_option linter.regula false and regula.localFoundation never waive it: lake lint, the build-lint policy target and axiomGate still apply the rule. Where Regula's local linter reports a finding during a project build (axiomGate and the policy target keep it on by default; lake lint builds with it off, whatever the source sets linter.regula to), that finding is a build warning, so the result is INCOMPLETE under RG2003 instead of carrying this rule's finding. Switching the local linter off changes which finding is reported, never whether the result is accepted. Hiding the diagnostic does not establish the property it checks.\n\nRegistration is @[regula_material] from Regula.MaterialClaim. Removing a registration from a material declaration changes the reviewed claim, not only this rule's result.\n\nProject enforcement runs through lake lint (incremental), lake lint -- --fresh and lake exe axiomGate (fresh whole-project audits from empty build output), and the build-lint policy target. See the adoption guide.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG5002: Registered public material declarations require docstrings","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/RG5002/#RG5002-configuration"}});